&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Physical AI team at CoreWeave is building the compute foundation for the next era of AI, operating the world&#39;s leading specialised AI cloud. We focus on one of the highest-conviction bets in the company: architecting and delivering the distributed systems and real-time infrastructure that underpin simulation-driven autonomous or embodied AI at hyperscale. Our team operates at the intersection of advanced cloud infrastructure and applied deep tech—exactly where conventional architectures break down.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Principal Architect for Hyperscale Simulation Software, you will have founding-team-level influence and hold ultimate responsibility for the commercial success of CoreWeave’s product offering in hyperscale simulation, digital twins, and embodied AI training workloads. You will define the overarching product and technical strategy, shaping the roadmap for GPU-based simulation alongside product, research, and commercial stakeholders. This hands-on technical leadership role requires you to lead architectural decisions across the full stack—from bare-metal GPU/CPU topology through orchestration layers to application-facing APIs (particularly software offerings by NVIDIA). You will directly partner with enterprise customers and strategic accounts to translate platform capabilities into deployed, high-value solutions that generate substantial revenue and place CoreWeave at the forefront of the industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of founding, leading, or acting as an early architect of deep-tech platforms that successfully reached commercial deployment (e.g., AI/ML, simulation, digital twins, or defence systems).

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Impact at LILA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lila Sciences is seeking a Research Engineer, Scientific Computing and ML/Physics Infrastructure to help turn promising research tools into robust, scalable systems. This role bridges research and production: you will work with scientists and ML researchers who can prototype useful tools, then help make those tools efficient, distributed, fault tolerant, and usable across Lila&#39;s compute environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Molecular Intelligence team is building ML and physics-based infrastructure for drug discovery, including biophysics workflows, computational chemistry tools, cofolding models, low-data learning systems, simulation workflows, and agent-usable scientific pipelines. We need an engineer who can improve code quality, architecture, GPU efficiency, cluster portability, and operational reliability without slowing down research velocity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Building&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take research tools, prototypes, and scientific workflows developed by scientists or academic-style researchers and make them scalable, efficient, and maintainable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate directly with computational biophysics, computational chemistry, and machine learning scientists to turn research workflows into scalable agent-usable systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and support ML and physics infrastructure for model training, molecular simulation, data processing, and agent-executed scientific workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure workflows run reliably across multiple clusters and compute environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve GPU utilization, distributed execution, throughput, fault tolerance, and reproducibility for ML and scientific workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect larger-scale systems around research code, including job orchestration, retry behavior, monitoring, artifact handling, and workflow traceability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize ML, physics, and pipeline code for performance and scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain development and execution environments across local, cloud, and GPU-based systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Package scientific tools into reusable services, workflows, or APIs that can be used by researchers, pipelines, and AI agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with research, platform, and infrastructure teams to bridge exploratory scientific work with reliable engineering systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document systems clearly and establish pragmatic engineering patterns for research teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
